From 45b3b4d56ec16c9142f62b54fe5269bbca08de2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gaia <build@heygaia.io>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 07:05:11 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(js): service workers only in secure contexts, and a
 registration's ready settles

navigator.serviceWorker existed on every document and isSecureContext did
not exist at all; in Chrome the container is [SecureContext], absent on a
plain-http, about:blank or data: document. isSecureContext now follows the
document URL (https, wss, file, loopback http; a blob: URL by its origin;
an about:blank or srcdoc frame by its parent, and a frame only inside a
secure parent), and the container is exposed only where it is true.

A registration stayed workerless and navigator.serviceWorker.ready never
settled, so a page that waits on ready before using the registration
stalled forever. No worker script runs here, so a registered worker is
modelled as one with no event handlers: it is active at once, ready
resolves for a page inside its scope, and it handles no fetches or
messages.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tm2SNEJ42hMPiZ6cFb8Vih
---
 crates/obscura-js/js/bootstrap.js | 79 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 crates/obscura-js/src/runtime.rs  | 42 +++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 108 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/crates/obscura-js/js/bootstrap.js b/crates/obscura-js/js/bootstrap.js
index 7e222fa..3eac80f 100644
--- a/crates/obscura-js/js/bootstrap.js
+++ b/crates/obscura-js/js/bootstrap.js
